    "fullDesc": "Learn how to organize, query and analyze structured business data using SQL and PostgreSQL—without requiring previous programming experience. This practical SQL & Relational Database Fundamentals course introduces relational database concepts, tables, data types, primary keys, foreign keys and SQL query development. Start by learning to retrieve and filter data using SELECT, WHERE, ORDER BY, DISTINCT, LIMIT and conditional expressions. Develop confidence in combining information across related tables with INNER JOIN, LEFT JOIN and multi-table queries. Learn to produce business reports using aggregate functions, GROUP BY, HAVING, CASE expressions, subqueries and Common Table Expressions. Explore introductory window functions for ranking and comparing records without losing individual row detail. Build reliable relational databases using CREATE TABLE, ALTER TABLE, constraints and safe INSERT, UPDATE and DELETE operations. Understand transaction fundamentals, database integrity, indexing awareness and the importance of parameterized queries when SQL is used inside applications. Use PostgreSQL with DBeaver or pgAdmin to work on realistic admissions, retail sales or inventory datasets. Complete a portfolio-ready relational database project containing a documented schema, sample data, at least 20 meaningful SQL queries, a data-quality checklist and a business reporting summary. The programme emphasizes practical SQL reasoning, reliable query results, data relationships and business interpretation—not simply memorizing SQL commands.",
